Subject: Cantor Runtime, Process Procedure, and FPGA Dual-Hemisphere Review

Description: Projection-and-critique review that tests the strongest useful architecture against the strongest skeptical case before canonical authority.

@ [review_uuid] f263a98b-78e6-4ca0-9af5-80677b7b73c1
@ [explosion] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Cantor_Runtime_Procedure_FPGA_Seven_Fold_Exhaustion_2026-08-05.sop
@ [constraints] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Cantor_Runtime_Procedure_FPGA_Constraint_Ledger_2026-08-05.sop

& [ProjectiveHemisphere] states the strongest promise
  + recurring inference behaviors can become inspectable typed procedures instead of repeatedly improvised prose
  + exact SOP anchors can make model/tool deliberation portable across providers and sessions
  + deterministic replay can expose which proposal, rule, message, or version changed an outcome
  + named process roles and token-ring stability can coordinate multiple models without claiming a shared mind
  + one canonical IR can support interpreter, WASM, native software, FPGA interpreter, and native FPGA experiments
  + FPGA acceleration could make high-volume graph lookup, scoring, digest, routing, barrier, and trace kernels low-latency and power-efficient
  + separate phase receipts can make model-generated helper procedures useful without treating generation as authority

& [CriticalHemisphere] states the strongest objections
  + the system may become more complex than ordinary tool calling and a relational or graph database require
  + Simula terminology may romanticize a historical language without improving the actual compiler or runtime
  + deterministic procedures can reproduce a wrong premise perfectly and create false confidence
  + a token ring can converge on a shared error, deadlock, or reward conformity over useful dissent
  + model-generated code expands injection, denial-of-service, covert-channel, and confused-deputy surfaces
  + a canonical IR can prematurely freeze semantics and make future refinement expensive
  + FPGA work is speculative without profiles showing software lookup or routing is a bottleneck
  + HLS or RTL toolchains add long compilation cycles, vendor coupling, difficult debugging, and substantial verification burden
  + storing every trace may expose sensitive inputs or create retention cost without improving decisions
  + an external tool boundary does not literally participate inside one uninterrupted transformer forward pass

& [Reconciliation] preserves value without accepting overclaim
  + begin with typed machine forms and a deterministic in-memory interpreter, not textual syntax polish or hardware
  + call the language Simula-inspired only where process identity, event ordering, passivation, and reactivation materially map
  + keep truth, evidence, authority, agreement, determinism, and performance as separate evaluated dimensions
  + require objections, qualifications, timeouts, and residuals in the negotiation protocol
  + admit only effectless bounded candidates in the first procedure experiment
  + version the IR narrowly and require explicit migration rather than claiming permanent universality
  + sign FPGA only as a non-executable eligibility and correspondence contract
  + require measured profiling and a target-specific SJS addendum before hardware implementation
  + apply sensitivity and retention policies to inputs, outputs, messages, and traces
  + describe shared inference as structured multi-pass coordination and not hidden-state co-execution

& [DecisionSet] is adopted
  + DEC-RPF-001 three authority surfaces instead of one
  + DEC-RPF-002 software-first reference semantics
  + DEC-RPF-003 semantic forms and canonical IR before textual syntax
  + DEC-RPF-004 effectless two-process experiment before general procedures
  + DEC-RPF-005 exact token-ring generation semantics with dissent and timeout preserved
  + DEC-RPF-006 independent Observer admission after validation, compilation, and verification
  + DEC-RPF-007 optional FPGA interpreter and native realization remain future alternatives
  + DEC-RPF-008 no hardware frontier without profiling and target-specific authority

& [InvalidationAndReroute] are explicit
  + reroute to ordinary tool functions when procedure forms add no replay, governance, reuse, or coordination value
  + reroute to a graph or relational query planner when the subject is retrieval only
  + reroute from token ring when measured deliberation quality is worse than independent proposals plus Observer synthesis
  + revise IR when two independently useful procedures cannot be represented without unsafe escape hatches
  + abandon FPGA target when software meets latency, throughput, power, determinism, and isolation needs
  + invalidate any authority if implementation pressure requires live effects, hidden mutable state, or unbounded behavior not processed here

& [ReviewDisposition] is pass_with_bounded_authority
  + the critical case changes sequencing, claims, and gates but does not defeat the effectless deterministic experiments
  + no present evidence justifies executable FPGA work
